     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Oct 21, 2016 at 6:37 AM, John McKown <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">john.arch...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">On Thu, Oct 20, 2016 at 8:41 PM, lily li </span><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">choc...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> wrote:</span><br></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi ggplot users,<div><br></div><div>I want to put an equation inside of the plot, but don&#39;t know how to make an upper case.</div><div>How to make the R2 have upper case 2? Thanks.</div><div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\">​​</div>figure1 = ggplot()+</div><div>    geom_point(data=DF, aes(x=day, y=temp))+</div><div>    annotate(&#39;text&#39;, x=5, y=2, label=&#39;y= ax + b, R2=0.95&#39;)</div><div>print(figure1)</div></div></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br></font></span></blockquote><div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\">​Rather than &quot;upper case 2&quot;, I think you mean &quot;superscript 2&quot; (as in R-squared or R² ). The superscript 2 character is unicode charater U+00B2. In the normal R CLI on Windows 7 Professional (at work), I was able to put in the </div><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">²<div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\">​ by holding down the &lt;ALT&gt; key while pressing the ​0178 keys in that order, then releasing the &lt;ALT&gt; key. But, perhaps better, is to use &quot;R\\u{00B2}&quot;. If I have indeed understood what you want, please try:</div></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\"><br></div></span></div><div><span><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\">​</div>figure1 = ggplot()+</div><div>    geom_point(data=DF, aes(x=day, y=temp))+</div></span><div><span>    annotate(&#39;text&#39;, x=5, y=2, label=&#39;y= ax + b, R</span><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;display:inline\">​\\u{00B2}​</div>=0.95&#39;)</div><div>print(figure1)</div></div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:19.5px\">Heisenberg may have been here.</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:19.5px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:19.5px\">Unicode: </span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;line-height:19.5px\"><a href=\"http://xkcd.com/1726/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow